(2246235, 306414, 37893, '<td valign="top">Woohoo! Thanks everyone for the yellow! Willy The Worm thanks you as well. Just in case you were wondering, Willy wasn''t harmed in the making of this shoot. After a solid dose of buttery taste from using PAM on the apple, he lies in rest inside his container amongst his brothers inside my fridge until the next time he is called for another act.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Woohoo! Thanks everyone for the yellow! Willy The Worm thanks you as well. Just in case you were wondering, Willy wasn''t harmed in the making of this shoot. After a solid dose of buttery taste from using PAM on the apple, he lies in rest inside his container amongst his brothers inside my fridge until the next time he is called for another act. ', '2006-03-22 01:25:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(2246240, 306757, 39141, '<td valign="top">Thank you for the excellent comments and scores. Im sorry I didnt have the time to vote in this challenge.<br/> I later regretted using this title - the song to which it might allude is wrong for the innocence of the girls. <br/>The cut off feet is the biggest dissappointment - gotta take more care - the picture will never happen again. I agree that it needs more light from the left but I would never use a flash fill in this situation, The girls knew I was shooting but I was being as unobtrusive as possible, I had the little camera on my knee while they were watching their teacher be introduced to two of my students (we are working on a community project across the road). The girl on the left is Carolina (pronounced eena), her mother helps cook for us. <br/>I guess I wanted to be a bit like Henri Cartier-Bresson in the neighbourhood with his quiet little Leica rangefinder. <br/>Im glad some people liked this a lot - I do. There are two other pics from this day that may be technically better and just as engaging that I will post in a month or so when I get home and work on them.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-03-22 01:29:01.</i></td>', 'Thank you for the excellent comments and scores. Im sorry I didnt have the time to vote in this challenge. I later regretted using this title - the song to which it might allude is wrong for the innocence of the girls. The cut off feet is the biggest dissappointment - gotta take more care - the picture will never happen again. I agree that it needs more light from the left but I would never use a flash fill in this situation, The girls knew I was shooting but I was being as unobtrusive as possible, I had the little camera on my knee while they were watching their teacher be introduced to two of my students (we are working on a community project across the road). The girl on the left is Carolina (pronounced eena), her mother helps cook for us. I guess I wanted to be a bit like Henri Cartier-Bresson in the neighbourhood with his quiet little Leica rangefinder. Im glad some people liked this a lot - I do. There are two other pics from this day that may be technically better and just as engaging that I will post in a month or so when I get home and work on them.', '2006-03-22 01:28:00.000000', '2006-03-22 01:29:01.000000', 0),
(2246249, 306414, 15266, '<td valign="top">Supreme image, Rikki!  You are da man and I am pond scum!  An excellent, creative studio shot! And for the extra effort - totally paid off.</td>', 'Supreme image, Rikki!  You are da man and I am pond scum!  An excellent, creative studio shot! And for the extra effort - totally paid off.', '2006-03-22 01:31:36.000000', NULL, 0),
