(2247109, 306489, 24846, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on your red. Yesterday I was reading a tutorial by <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/how.php?HOW_ID=40" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">mandy </a>on 1/2 face technique. This is a prime example of excellent work.</td>', 'Congratulations on your red. Yesterday I was reading a tutorial by mandy on 1/2 face technique. This is a prime example of excellent work.', '2006-03-22 12:10:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(2247168, 305883, 5112, '<td valign="top">Beautiful shot.  I love the patterns of the upside-down chairs and the light on the wall.  I like the shadow that looks like a high heel shoe towards the left on the wall.  I like the treatment, it''s very appropriate for the image.<br/> <br/>Congratulations BTW on an excellent finish.  7th place (and almost 6.7 score) is great!<br/> <br/>It''s always hard to give an opinion on what you might not like about an image, because you''re putting yourself on the line.  You asked what could have been done differently, what didn''t work.<br/> <br/>In my opinion the image is a bit too busy.  In particular the top 1/6th to 1/8th of the picture (the window and the tops of the chalkboards) doesn''t add that much to the image, while at the same time taking away quite a bit of its mystery.  To my eyes the image is stronger without that top section.<br/> <br/>I also think that even though this is obviously a classroom (thus, education), the connection to "education" is not super strong.  It doesn''t scream education; it screams good old times, memories, stuff like that, but not education.<br/> <br/>And last, the light is beautiful, but it is somewhat harsh.  If there were a way to capture the same image with some dust in the air, or something to make the light softer, more voluptuous, I think the image would sing a better song.  I suppose some of this could be done in post-processing, but IMO nothing beats the real thing, and it would be so much fun to actually capture a softer, more diffused but still very evening directional light in this place.<br/> <br/>Hope this helps :)<br/> <br/>~ursula<br/></td>', 'Beautiful shot.  I love the patterns of the upside-down chairs and the light on the wall.  I like the shadow that looks like a high heel shoe towards the left on the wall.  I like the treatment, it''s very appropriate for the image. Congratulations BTW on an excellent finish.  7th place (and almost 6.7 score) is great! It''s always hard to give an opinion on what you might not like about an image, because you''re putting yourself on the line.  You asked what could have been done differently, what didn''t work. In my opinion the image is a bit too busy.  In particular the top 1/6th to 1/8th of the picture (the window and the tops of the chalkboards) doesn''t add that much to the image, while at the same time taking away quite a bit of its mystery.  To my eyes the image is stronger without that top section. I also think that even though this is obviously a classroom (thus, education), the connection to "education" is not super strong.  It doesn''t scream education; it screams good old times, memories, stuff like that, but not education. And last, the light is beautiful, but it is somewhat harsh.  If there were a way to capture the same image with some dust in the air, or something to make the light softer, more voluptuous, I think the image would sing a better song.  I suppose some of this could be done in post-processing, but IMO nothing beats the real thing, and it would be so much fun to actually capture a softer, more diffused but still very evening directional light in this place. Hope this helps :) ~ursula', '2006-03-22 12:37:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(2247170, 304593, 14603, '<td valign="top">Great image..even though it`s obviously not a selective desat, it does have that feel due to the image being largely red and grey.<br/> <br/>Tell the truth Ed...you`re a closet desat man :)<br/> <br/>Not surprised to see the teacher getting tough on anyone taking pics,I know from experience(taking sports shots at schools) that some children`s parents expressly forbid their kids from having their pictures taken..even in team shots.<br/>Makes me wonder what kind of home life they have and how many hang-ups and phobias they will end up carrying with them through life.<br/> <br/>Rant over, it only remains for me to congratulate you on your Blue.<br/>Well Done.</td>', 'Great image..even though it`s obviously not a selective desat, it does have that feel due to the image being largely red and grey. Tell the truth Ed...you`re a closet desat man :) Not surprised to see the teacher getting tough on anyone taking pics,I know from experience(taking sports shots at schools) that some children`s parents expressly forbid their kids from having their pictures taken..even in team shots.Makes me wonder what kind of home life they have and how many hang-ups and phobias they will end up carrying with them through life. Rant over, it only remains for me to congratulate you on your Blue.Well Done.', '2006-03-22 12:38:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(2247266, 305617, 33182, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Gene L.:</b></div><hr/><i> Too bad they are so dirty (yeah I know, winter weather). The yellow would make a bright color study if they had just been washed :-) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Dirty, Those aren''t dirty. Let me go to work and I''ll take a picture of a dirty bus (I drive a school bus in the afternoons). &lt;g&gt;</td>', 'Originally posted by Gene L.: Too bad they are so dirty (yeah I know, winter weather). The yellow would make a bright color study if they had just been washed :-)   Dirty, Those aren''t dirty. Let me go to work and I''ll take a picture of a dirty bus (I drive a school bus in the afternoons). <g>', '2006-03-22 13:07:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(2247296, 304593, 54885, '<td valign="top">i just loved this and i gave it a 10! now as far as critiquing i will just leave that to the experts on this digital photog club</td>', 'i just loved this and i gave it a 10! now as far as critiquing i will just leave that to the experts on this digital photog club', '2006-03-22 13:14:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(2247333, 306926, 30049, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by glad2badad:</b></div><hr/><i> Very creative concept.  A little hot (overexposed) - this would have scored higher if it wasn''t.  5 from me for creativity, could have been an 8.  Hopefully I''m an anomaly.  ;^)  Good luck in the challenge. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>I should have kept the score a secret?  I''m the only one not marked helpful.  :(</td>', 'Originally posted by glad2badad: Very creative concept.  A little hot (overexposed) - this would have scored higher if it wasn''t.  5 from me for creativity, could have been an 8.  Hopefully I''m an anomaly.  ;^)  Good luck in the challenge.  I should have kept the score a secret?  I''m the only one not marked helpful.  :(', '2006-03-22 13:22:54.000000', NULL, 0),
