(2250543, 305883, 26633, '<td valign="top">This was in my top four in this challenge. I thought the patterns created on the wall by the light streaking through the window were worhty of a picture in their own right. The upturned chairs, neglected walls and the blackboard on the wall all gave a nostalgic feel to the picture. Additionally I thought the toning and the handling of the tonal range were very good.</td>', 'This was in my top four in this challenge. I thought the patterns created on the wall by the light streaking through the window were worhty of a picture in their own right. The upturned chairs, neglected walls and the blackboard on the wall all gave a nostalgic feel to the picture. Additionally I thought the toning and the handling of the tonal range were very good.', '2006-03-23 08:26:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(2250880, 306414, 42125, '<td valign="top">This is a great photo, nice and crisp focus, the lighting is good and good use of both horizontal and vertical thirds!<br/> <br/>For those who do not know, the worm actually never goes inside the apple, only comes out of it!!!. So If you have an appletree and don''t want any worms, take care of it before the flowers turn into apples because at that time the insect lays its eggs.<br/>Also if you see a hole in an apple it is probably ok to eat it because then you know the worm has already left.<br/> <br/>Gratulations!<br/> <br/></td>', 'This is a great photo, nice and crisp focus, the lighting is good and good use of both horizontal and vertical thirds! For those who do not know, the worm actually never goes inside the apple, only comes out of it!!!. So If you have an appletree and don''t want any worms, take care of it before the flowers turn into apples because at that time the insect lays its eggs.Also if you see a hole in an apple it is probably ok to eat it because then you know the worm has already left. Gratulations! ', '2006-03-23 11:25:39.000000', NULL, 0),
